{"title":"Career Roadmap · Laser Systems Engineer","role":"Laser Systems Engineer","summary":"A Laser Systems Engineer designs, develops, tests, integrates and maintains laser-based systems. The field combines optics, photonics, electronics, materials, control systems, signal processing and software.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. (Bachelor of Technology / Engineering)","Course":"Optoelectronics / Photonics Engineering"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Laser Systems Engineer designs, develops, tests, integrates and maintains laser-based systems. The field combines optics, photonics, electronics, materials, control systems, signal processing and software."},{"type":"p","text":"Typical applications include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Industrial laser processing"},{"text":"Laser manufacturing"},{"text":"Optical communications"},{"text":"Medical lasers"},{"text":"Semiconductor manufacturing"},{"text":"Scientific instrumentation"},{"text":"LiDAR"},{"text":"Defence and aerospace"},{"text":"Spectroscopy"},{"text":"Metrology"},{"text":"Imaging"},{"text":"Quantum technologies"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A strong graduate should understand the complete laser system rather than only laser physics:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Laser Source","Optical Components","Beam Conditioning","Modulation / Control","Target / Sample","Detector","Signal Processing","Control / Measurement"]},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest positioning is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Laser Physics","Optics","Photonics","Optoelectronics","Optical Testing","Control Systems","Embedded Electronics","Python/Data Analysis"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Career Flow"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Tech / B.E. Photonics / Optoelectronics","Physics + Mathematics + Electronics","Geometrical & Physical Optics","Laser Physics","Optoelectronic Devices","Optical Measurement & Instrumentation